cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this development, please cite it as below."
title: "Exact contact numbers for packings of six to nine congruent balls: a Lean 4 formalization"
abstract: >-
  A machine-checked proof that the contact numbers of packings of n congruent balls
  in Euclidean 3-space satisfy c(n,3) = 3n - 6 for n = 6, 7, 8, 9, and that every
  packing attaining these values is minimally rigid. This settles the numerical half
  of Conjecture 5.2 of Bezdek and Khan, and its structural half at every n for which
  that conjecture asserts a value. Formalized in Lean 4 on top of mathlib.
type: software
